	{
		"id": "dark",
		"title": "why track 3 is dark",
		"about": "the sound read, the cause and the fix",
		"model": "recorded",
		"turns": [
			{
				"user": "why does track 3 sound so dark?",
				"conductor": [
					{
						"tools": [
							{
								"id": "toolu_01TrJtrKDprrZ7QBFTq7c5Az",
								"name": "read_sound",
								"input": {
									"track": 3
								}
							}
						]
					},
					{
						"tools": [],
						"text": "The filter cutoff on track 3 is at 00. That closes the svf lowpass almost completely, so only the darkest part of the sound gets through. The filter envelope (env amount 33) opens it a little on each note, but not by much.\n\nTo brighten it, raise the cutoff:\n\n1. `T3`, then `M3`\n2. `turn E1` clockwise. Try around 40–60 and adjust by ear.\n\nIf you want the filter to snap open on each note instead, raise env amount with `turn E3` on the same page."
					}
				],
				"subagent": []
			}
		]
	},
	{
		"id": "pump",
		"title": "make the bass pump",
		"about": "a duck set up on the replica",
		"model": "recorded",
		"turns": [
			{
				"user": "make the bass pump with the kick",
				"conductor": [
					{
						"tools": [
							{
								"id": "toolu_018vj7Yysg39mTU2oHd9nsxs",
								"name": "device_status",
								"input": {}
							}
						]
					},
					{
						"tools": [
							{
								"id": "toolu_01E7CnfT2HxArsGyuSGDEJTH",
								"name": "plan_steps",
								"input": {
									"show": true,
									"track": 3,
									"settings": [
										{
											"param": "lfo type",
											"value": "duck"
										},
										{
											"param": "duck source",
											"value": "1"
										},
										{
											"param": "lfo amount",
											"value": 70
										},
										{
											"param": "duck hold",
											"value": 10
										},
										{
											"param": "duck release",
											"value": 40
										}
									]
								}
							}
						],
						"text": "Track 3 is the bass and track 1 the drums. I'll set the duck on the bass with track 1 as its source."
					},
					{
						"tools": [],
						"text": "The bass on track 3 now ducks on the replica whenever track 1 plays. I set the duck LFO on `M4` like this:\n\n- **Source:** track 1, the drums.\n- **Amount:** about 70, a clear dip.\n- **Hold:** short, so the dip is tight.\n- **Release:** about 40, so the bass swells back between hits.\n\nThe patterns are empty at the moment, so you won't hear it until track 1 and track 3 have notes.\n\nTrack 1 also carries the hats, so the bass will dip on every hat as well as every kick. For a pump on the kick only, put the kick on its own drum track (track 2) and set the source to that track. Or set the source to the metronome, which dips the bass on every beat.\n\nTo undo it, use `shift + M4` on track 3 and pick another LFO type.\n\nI can write a beat and a bassline so you can hear it if you like.\n\n[instrument.lfo-duck] [howto.sidechain-duck]"
					}
				],
				"subagent": []
			}
		]
	},
